&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="-results"&gt;📈 Results
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3 id="-normalized-throughput-per-vcpu"&gt;🎯 Normalized Throughput per vCPU
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Intel Xeon 6 processor-powered &lt;strong&gt;C4&lt;/strong&gt; consistently outperforms &lt;strong&gt;C3&lt;/strong&gt; with &lt;strong&gt;1.4x to 1.7×
throughput per-vCPU&lt;/strong&gt; across batch sizes up to 64.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Formula&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;normalized_throughput_per_vCPU = (throughput_C4 / vCPUs_C4) / (throughput_C3 / vCPUs_C3)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Intel/blog/resolve/main/gpt-oss-on-intel-xeon/throughput-gpt-oss-per-vcpu.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="Throughput per vCPU"
&gt;
&lt;em&gt;C4 demonstrates consistent 1.4x-1.7x throughput advantage per vCPU across all batch sizes&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="-cost--tco-analysis"&gt;💰 Cost &amp;amp; TCO Analysis
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;At batch size 64, &lt;strong&gt;C4&lt;/strong&gt; delivers &lt;strong&gt;1.7× per-vCPU throughput&lt;/strong&gt; compared to &lt;strong&gt;C3&lt;/strong&gt;. With near
price parity per vCPU, this yields a &lt;strong&gt;1.7× TCO advantage&lt;/strong&gt; - C3 would require 1.7× the spending
for equivalent generated token volume.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TCO Calculation&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;throughput_ratio = 1.7 ⇒ TCO_C3/TCO_C4 ≈ 1.7&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://huggingface.co/datasets/Intel/blog/resolve/main/gpt-oss-on-intel-xeon/throughput-gpt-oss-per-dollar.png"
loading="lazy"
alt="Throughput per Dollar"
&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Cost efficiency comparison shows C4&amp;rsquo;s superior performance per dollar invested&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
